    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with an aggressive stance, led by **Kyle Tucker** (81.11) and **Andy Pages** (74.84), who headline our lineup against Merrill Kelly. The massive boost in their respective efficiency scores is fueled by Kelly\u2019s porous 5.13 xERA and favorable park conditions, making both essential anchors for our HR and RBI production. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.10) also emerges as a premier play; he faces Tyler Mahle in a matchup where his dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) and the high-leverage #4 hole in the lineup maximize his scoring ceiling. While **Nasim Nunez** (66.19) lacks the raw power of the outfield core, his ability to exploit the high xERA of Petty makes him a vital start for those hunting scarce SB totals.\n\nOur most difficult selection decision involved **Luis Lara**, whose 47.02 score nearly cracked the lineup. He was ultimately bypassed due to the higher projected efficiency and run-scoring potential of the starters surrounding him in the batting order. Similarly, **Coby Mayo** was considered but pulled back, failing to clear our 40.0 \"Zebras Floor\" due to a difficult matchup against Eovaldi and an unfavorable platoon split. As we finalize the roster, note that **Jorge Polanco** (50.23) carries the highest variance on the day; while he holds a respectable projection, the 40% rain risk in his contest is a legitimate threat that could truncate his game and jeopardize his ability to accumulate counting stats. We are also monitoring **Liam Hicks**, **Andy Pages**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Jackson Merrill**, all of whom are currently tagged with \"Lineup Pending\" status; should their confirmed batting positions shift significantly downward, their efficiency scores will be reassessed.",
